<title>ITALY: Stet details offer for s/holders' opt-out.</title>
<headline>Stet details offer for s/holders' opt-out.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders in Italian state telecoms holding STET who do not want to keep their shares for a merger with Telecom Italia will be offered 6,466.18 lire per ordinary, Stet chairman Guido Rossi said.</p>
<p>Rossi, speaking an extraordinary shareholder meeting in Turin, said the price for savings shares would be 4,976.60 lire.</p>
<p>Stet and Telecom Italia are due to merge by June and the resulting company will be privatised later in the year.</p>
</text>
